  "title": "Normalize: one 'Re-normalize…' sheet on web and iOS that asks which operations to run",
  "description": "Depends on normalize-1 (the op registry and POST /api/recipes/{id}/normalize). \
Replace the per-operation menu items (iOS RecipeDetailView: Enrich with AI, Auto-Rename, Generate Description, Rescrape from Source; web ViewRecipePage and the CookbookBulkToolbar bulk actions) with one 'Re-normalize…' action that opens a sheet listing the ops from the server's op list, grouped as Source (Re-fetch from source, Re-extract from saved page) and Normalize (title, description, tags, ingredient names, house style when it lands), plus Photo if those ops join the registry. \
Behavior: defaults to the user's normal import set; checking Re-fetch checks and locks Re-extract; ops unavailable for the recipe are disabled with the reason (no source URL, no stored capture); if the recipe has hand edits since its last source-derived version and a source op is checked, the sheet says those edits will be replaced. \
Progress shows per op from the job's steps, and when it finishes the client offers the before/after version diff. \
The same sheet works on a multi-selection in the web cookbook (and iOS if it gets bulk selection), running the bulk endpoint. \
'Customize with AI' (customize-1) stays a separate action since it takes free text. \
'Generate AI photo' can stay its own menu item if it doesn't become an op. \
Both clients; no data/ diffs expected.",
